                "label": "Grammar: Common Errors in the Use of Prepositions",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "q": "What are the nine common types of preposition errors given in the book?",
                    "a": "1. Wrong Preposition Choice — She is married with a doctor. / She is married to a doctor. 2. Unnecessary Preposition — Where are you going to? / Where are you going? 3. Omission of Necessary Preposition — He is responsible paying the bills. / He is responsible for paying the bills. 4. Confusion Between Similar Prepositions — She is good in English. / She is good at English. 5. Incorrect Pairing in Phrasal Verbs — He insisted for an answer. / He insisted on an answer. 6. Preposition with Time Expressions — She was born at 1999. / She was born in 1999. ('Born' uses 'in' for years and 'on' for specific dates.) 7. Preposition with Place Expressions — He is in the bus. / He is on the bus. ('On' is used for public transport, not 'in'.) 8. Preposition with Adjectives — She is afraid from dogs. / She is afraid of dogs. 9. Preposition with Verbs — I prefer coffee than tea. / I prefer coffee to tea."
                  }
                ]
