                    "a": "The Rh blood system is represented by +ve or -ve sign, which refers to the presence or absence of the Rh antigen on the surface of the red blood cells. The antigen was observed in the Rhesus monkey by Landsteiner in the 1930s. The prime gene locus D is mainly responsible for the production of the Rh antigen; the human population has two alleles of D, D and d, and D is completely dominant over d. A person with genotype DD or Dd produces the Rh antigen and is called Rh+ve, while a person with genotype dd cannot produce the Rh antigen and is called Rh-ve.",
                    "q": "What is the Rh blood system? How are Rh+ve and Rh-ve persons determined?"
