                    "a": "Unlike the naturally occurring anti-A and anti-B antibodies of the ABO system, anti-Rh antibody production requires a stimulus by the human Rh antigen itself. If an Rh-ve person receives blood of an Rh+ve person, the recipient begins to produce anti-Rh antibodies against the Rh antigen and destroys the donor's red blood cells (clumping). On the other hand, Rh-ve blood, which does not contain any anti-Rh antibody, can be transfused to an Rh+ve recipient.",
