                    "a": "Copper is refined by electrolysis in an electrolytic tank. Thick plates of blister copper serve as the anode and thin sheets of pure copper act as the cathode. The electrolyte is copper sulphate acidified with sulphuric acid. At the anode copper is oxidized (Cu → Cu+2 + 2e-) and at the cathode Cu+2 ions are reduced and deposited as pure copper (Cu+2 + 2e- → Cu). Impurities fall to the bottom as anode mud.",
