                    "a": "(i) Toluene to p-nitrobenzoic acid: First nitrate toluene with mixed acid (conc. HNO3 + conc. H2SO4) to get a mixture of o- and p-nitrotoluene; separate the p-isomer, then oxidize its -CH3 group with alkaline KMnO4 (followed by acidification) to -COOH.\nC6H5CH3 → (conc. HNO3, conc. H2SO4) p-O2N-C6H4-CH3 → (KMnO4, then H+) p-O2N-C6H4-COOH (p-nitrobenzoic acid)\n(ii) Benzene to m-nitrotoluene: First nitrate benzene to nitrobenzene, then carry out Friedel-Crafts methylation with CH3Cl/AlCl3. Since -NO2 is a meta directing group, the -CH3 group enters the meta position.\nC6H6 → (conc. HNO3, conc. H2SO4) C6H5NO2 → (CH3Cl, AlCl3) m-O2N-C6H4-CH3 (m-nitrotoluene)",
