                    "a": "(b) Ketone ✓\nA secondary alcohol is first oxidized to a ketone (the intermediate). Under vigorous oxidation with acidified dichromate the ketone can be further oxidized with cleavage of a C-C bond to give a carboxylic acid (e.g. 2-propanol → acetone → ethanoic acid + CO2 + H2O). Under ordinary conditions the oxidation of a secondary alcohol stops at the ketone.",
