                    "a": "De Morgan's theorems state: (i) (A·B)′ = Ā + B̄ — the complement of a product is the sum of the complements. (ii) (A + B)′ = Ā·B̄ — the complement of a sum is the product of the complements. They are used to simplify Boolean expressions and to design circuits with NAND or NOR gates only.",
                    "q": "State De Morgan's theorems."
