                    "a": "A half adder adds two single bits and produces a sum (S = A⊕B) and a carry (C = A·B). A full adder adds three bits (two bits and a carry-in) and is made of two half adders and an OR gate. Adders are the building blocks of the arithmetic unit of a computer.",
                    "q": "What are half adder and full adder?"
